module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "readback_ordered_only_by_statement_position" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a readback is written after the effect it must follow and has no dependency edge to it, so in a pure graph it is not ordered after anything** (INVALID STATE: an effectful producer and an observation of its consequence are both bound in one function, the observation appearing later in the text, and the author reads that position as sequence. The substrate is a dependency graph: what orders two nodes is an EDGE, and a reading whose inputs do not include the effect's result has none. It may be evaluated on either side of the effect, or -- if its value is demanded before the effect's -- reliably BEFORE it. The observation is then of the state the effect was about to change, reported as the state the effect produced.)",

    "WHY IT IS NOT THE WALL-CLOCK SIBLING. [[collector_armed_after_the_transition_it_observes]] is an instrument started at the wrong MOMENT by a human or a script, and its repair is to arm the collector first. [[enforcement_gate_positioned_after_the_effect_it_guards]] is a refusal computed before and enforced after. This one is neither: the author DID write the observation after the effect, and would pass a reading of the code, because the defect is that writing it after is not saying anything in this language. The two siblings are about WHEN something ran; this is about a language in which when is not expressed by where.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Every value is correct in isolation and every type checks. The effect happens and the observation happens; the fault is that nothing relates them. The tell is a function that binds an effectful call and one or more readings whose arguments are all derived from the FUNCTION'S OWN PARAMETERS rather than from the effect's result -- an identity, a slot, a path, a slice name. A second tell is a record literal whose fields are one effect and several observations of it: the fields of a record have no order at all, so a reader looking for sequence there is reading punctuation.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-09-20 while writing gunbc.runner_microvm_lifecycle_realize observe_attempt_teardown. That fold builds one ObservedTeardown whose `stop` field performs the bounded stop of the attempt's VMM unit and whose `cgroup`, `mounts`, `attempt_storage` and `credential_disk` fields read the host back. Every readback took only the attempt, so the whole teardown proof -- no surviving processes, an empty cgroup subtree, the jail and the credential drive gone -- could have been taken against a cell whose VMM was still running, and would have been reported as the state after the stop. Nothing would have refused: a populated cgroup read before the stop is a perfectly well-formed CgroupSubtreePopulated, and the cell would have quarantined for residue that the stop was about to remove. The mirror case is worse and is the same defect: a resource absent before the guest created it reads as a clean teardown.",

    "THE REPAIR IS AN EDGE, AND THE EDGE IS ALSO THE SENTENCE. The stop is bound first and its ObservedStop is passed to every readback as a parameter named `after`. The readbacks do not otherwise consult it; the sequencing IS the use, and it is the only mechanism a dependency graph affords for it. A parameter that exists to order is not a decoration: in this substrate it is the word `after`, and removing it removes the ordering rather than removing noise.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, cheap and mechanical: for every observation whose meaning depends on an effect, ask which of its arguments could not have been computed before that effect ran. If the answer is none, it is not ordered after it. The question is asked of ARGUMENTS, not of line numbers, and it is the same question whether the two sit in one record literal, one block, or two functions.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- caught by an author re-deriving the slice, before any execution. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether an observation is causally downstream of an effect is decidable from the graph the compiler already holds: an effectful node and an observation of a subject that effect writes, with no path between them, is a refusable shape. What is missing is the SUBJECT relation -- the compiler knows `perform_bounded_stop` is effectful and knows `read_cell_cgroup_subtree` is effectful, and does not know they concern the same cell. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: effect subjects are modeled, so an effect declares what it writes and an observation declares what it reads, and the compiler refuses an unordered pair over one subject. Until that exists the wall is authorship and review, which is the rung this row claims and no higher.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
